/-!
# The unit axiom of a triple follows from the generation condition

Let `A = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} 𝒜 n` be a graded ring, `Y` a scheme, `L` an invertible `𝒪_Y`-module and
`ψ : A^{(d)} ⟶ Γ_*(Y, L)` a graded map in the degreewise spelling
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartFromRatios.VeroneseSections`, which records `ψ` as a
multiplicative family of additive maps and does not require `ψ(1) = 1`.

For a *triple* as in [Stacks, Tag 01N8], where `L` is in addition generated by the degree-`d`
values of `ψ` in the sense that their nonvanishing opens cover `Y`, the unit axiom `ψ(1) = 1`
holds.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTripleUnitSection.Triple.degreeZeroHom`: the ring map
  `A_0 ⟶ Γ(Y, 𝒪_Y)` of a triple.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTripleUnitSection.toFun_zero_eq_unitGlobal`: the degree-zero
  value of `ψ` at `1` is the unit section of `L^{⊗ 0}`, for a `ψ` satisfying the generation
  condition.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTripleUnitSection.Triple.psi_zero_eq_unitGlobal`: the same for a
  bundled triple.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NB)
* [Stacks Project, Section 01N4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N4)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite MonoidalCategory
open AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartFromRatios
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSectionsUnique (eq_of_smul_restrict_eq)
